      "Equine Blood Groups: Aa and Qa are the most antigenic and cause >90% of equine transfusion reactions and NI.",
      "Neonatal Isoerythrolysis (NI): Foal drinks maternal colostrum containing antibodies against paternal RBC antigens.",
      "Feline NI (Fading Kitten Syndrome): Type B queen mated to Type A tom; kittens ingest colostral anti-A antibodies.",
      "Bovine J Antigen: Plasma glycosphingolipid passively adsorbed onto erythrocyte surfaces after birth."
