    "clinical": "Veterinary Emergency Protocol: Systemic Anaphylaxis (Type I) is a life-threatening veterinary emergency. The drug of first choice is **Epinephrine (Adrenaline 1:1000 at 0.01 mg/kg IV or IM)**. Epinephrine acts on $\\beta_2$-adrenergic receptors on mast cells to elevate intracellular cyclic AMP (cAMP), immediately halting further mediator release while reversing lethal bronchospasm and restoring systemic arterial blood pressure.",
